    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d414">

                <pb facs="0483" n="423" sameAs="frus:frus1895p1/pg423"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Eustis to Mr. Uhl</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Embassy of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-06-06"><hi rendition="#italic">June 6, 1895</hi></date>.
                        (Received June 17.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 311.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Yesterday I had an interview with Mr.
                    Hanotaux and followed the instructions of your dispatch No. 424, of May 23, in
                    reference to the Venezuelan affair.</p>
                <pb facs="0484" n="424" xml:id="pg424"/>
                <p>He accepted my official statement with courtesy, but gave me no encouragement to
                    believe that the French Government would change its attitude.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">J. B. Eustis</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
